# act configuration – run CI locally against the kind cluster
#
# Usage:
#   act push                   # run the full CI pipeline
#   act push -j backend-tests  # run one job only
#   act push -j deploy         # build + deploy only
#
# act docs: https://nektosact.com/

# Use the medium ubuntu runner image – smallest image that has Docker CLI,
# Node 22 and Python 3.11 pre-installed.
# If you want the full GitHub-hosted environment use 'catthehacker/ubuntu:full-latest'
# (warning: ~60 GB download)
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Bind the host Docker socket into the act container so that docker build,
# kind create cluster, and kind load all work exactly as on real GitHub runners.
--bind
--container-daemon-socket /var/run/docker.sock

# Keep containers between jobs (faster re-runs)
--reuse
